		{
			"id": "109790100960594251",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@keithjgrant/109790100455743296",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J Grant",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@keithjgrant",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/298/456/496/421/823/original/4a1a35004ea6cec6.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-01T15:06:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I used to point and laugh at the chaos my back end teams took to get a Java code base configured and running.</p><p>Then I watched us repeat the exact same thing for the front end, each step along the way perfectly reasonable and addressing a very real problem, but the end result still turning into a complete mess.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109790104637229321",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.design/@jorge/109790104611141051",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hm… I’m skeptical",
				"url": "https://mastodon.design/@jorge",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/778/216/567/292/original/c06ae7de29b9c6a4.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-01T15:07:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Indeed. Good openness.</p><p>\"You can use React to build a single button, or you can use it to build an entire app.\"</p><p>You also, like, should NOT use it to build a single button, but that kind of position seems to be always missing from these retrospectives. There's  seems to be the underlying \"people are losing interest, so let's decide on the end-state of this so we can move to the next thing.\"</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109790167926745153",
			"parentId": "109790100960594251",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109790167926745153",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-01T15:23:33.528Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@keithjgrant\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>keithjgrant</span></a></span> it’s not uncommon to see overengineered solutions in our profession—but I do find it very odd that they achieve this level of ubiquity/success/investment!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
